cp|8|AT|^^
^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Some play a special form of |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=garbagestayman,Garbage Stayman^*N|CP||FP||at| which works as follows.|

n#|9|at|^^^fIf you do follow the link you can return  HERE  by clicking the  |fp|1|n#|3|at|@L|fp||n^|3|at|   icon button, top left.|
PG| ***** 20 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|If responder bids 2@C and opener responds 2@D, then if responder bids 2@H, that gives opener a choice of playing in either 2@H or 2@S and opener would pass with better hearts or bid 2@S with better spades.|
PG| ***** 21 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I often play that. However, you only employ |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?ndf=crawlingstayman,Crawling Stayman^*N|CP||FP||at| with 4-4 in the majors and a weak hand. With 5-4 you are almost always better off to transfer when you have a weak hand.|

n#|9|at|^^^fIf you do follow the link you can return  HERE  by clicking the  |fp|1|n#|3|at|@L|fp||n^|3|at|   icon button, top left.|
PG| ***** 22 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Occasionally you will miss a 4-4 fit and play in a 5-2 fit. But that doesn't happen often. More often you either play in an 8-card fit or a 5-2 fit rather than a 4-3 fit. And you prefer a 5-2 fit to a 4-3 fit. So the transfer was still the better bid here even if |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?ndf=crawlingstayman,Crawling Stayman^*N|CP||FP||at| was available.|

n#|9|at|^^^fIf you do follow the link you can return  HERE  by clicking the  |fp|1|n#|3|at|@L|fp||n^|3|at|   icon button, top left.|
PG| ***** 23 ***** |


