mb|P|mb|P|mb|1C|mb|1D|mb|1H|mb|2D|mb|3C|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Let's discuss West's options over 2@D for example 2@S. You might think that 2@S is a |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=reverses,Reverse^*N|CP||FP||at| but it really isn't (although it should show more than a min opener). So although with 6 clubs, I think 3@C is reasonable I also think 2@S is another option. That doesn't guarantee a really good hand, but just a decent hand with 5+ clubs and 4 spades.|
