nt|^z@3^b@2^^^B@2^*BA Kib: ^*NCan you elaborate on why the 2@S bid here would not be considered a |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=reverses,Reverse^*N|CP||FP||at|?|
PG| ***** 42 ***** |


cp|8|AT|^^
^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Because you are forcing the bidding to the 3-level you should not bid it with a really weak opener. However you can think of a |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=reverses,Reverse^*N|CP||FP||at| as "voluntarily" bidding past the two level in your first suit to bid a new suit.|
PG| ***** 43 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|For example if it goes 1@C-P-1@S-P-2@H, opener is voluntarily bypassing 2@C to bid 2@H and forcing the auction to a higher level. But on this auction, 2@C is not available to West. So 2@S is not technically a |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=reverses,Reverse^*N|CP||FP||at| Although as I said it should show at least a decent hand.|
PG| ***** 44 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|The reason I like it is because it is a bit more descriptive. However, as it turns out, it gives East a big problem as to what to bid over 2@S. Therefore, 3@C worked out better here.|
PG| ***** 45 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|With better clubs and worse spades I might prefer 3@C to 2@S.But with good but not great clubs and 3 honors in spades, I would have chosen 2@S.

|
PG| ***** 46 ***** |


