cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|It is true that 3@H is technically not a |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=lott,Law of Total Tricks^*N|CP||FP||at| bid since East is only promising 5 hearts. But pass is worse because, even with 6 hearts, East might not bid 3@H. Since East is promising 10 points, 3@H is likely to make even if they only have an 8-card fit. |
PG| ***** 63 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|So I think that West’s 3@H bid, although flawed, is better than pass. As it turns out, because East has 6 hearts, 3@H does follow the LOTT. 

|
