mb|1S|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I agree that 1@S is reasonable, although pass would have been okay. If you use Bergen ^*BAdjusted Points^*n to calculate the "points" part of the Rule of 20, West has 10 HCP and can add one for the quality 3 honor spade suit, giving him 11 points. With 9 cards in the majors West has 20 plus he has 2.5 quick tricks which is nice.|
PG| ***** 66 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|If the @DA had been the @HA instead, that is even a stronger case for opening the hand. Having all of your honors in your two longest suits is always worth an upgrade and means you should be more aggressive when you have a choice of actions.|
PG| ***** 67 ***** |


mb|P|mb|2C|mb|P|mb|2H|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|P|mb|2S|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Playing 2/1 GF, 2@S is forcing and is at least a mild slam try.|
PG| ***** 68 ***** |


mb|P|
