https://tinyurl.com/2653a3s5
qx|A6|st||rh||ah|Board 6 IMPs   -   On January 22, 2024|pn|hondo717,IraCT,Sputniks,danpsych|
md|4SQ432HAT6DQ984CT6,SK987H75DK53CJ872,SAJHKQ942D62CAKQ3,ST65HJ83DAJT7C954|sv|e|
mb|P|mb|P|mb|P|mb|1H|mb|P|mb|2H|mb|P3H|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|3@H is wrong for two reasons. The more important reason is that North is strong enough to bid 4@H. And advanced players don't play 3@H as invitational. They play that as competitive, meaning they really want to pass 2@H, but they know that against a good pair, East will balance since defending in 2 of a major when the points are evenly split, is rarely a good board.|
PG| ***** 107 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|So if the auction goes 1@H-P-2@H-P-3@H, that is just pre competing and is done with a weak hand with 6 hearts (LOTT) just to make it hard for the opponents to compete. It means you are being forehanded to prevent them to compete.If you want to invite game over 1@H-P-2@H, you bid a new suit.|
